What is a Pointer to Pointer (Double Pointer)
In C programming, pointers can store the address of other pointers too! Such pointers are called pointers to pointers or double pointers.
They are incredibly helpful in certain situations, such as when you need to modify the addresses stored in a pointer within a function.

Syntax of Double Pointer
type **ptr_name;

Why Do We Need Double Pointers?
#include<stdio.h;
int x = 10;
void changePointer(int **pp)
{
*pp = &x;
}
int main()
{
int *p = NULL;
changePointer(&p);
if(p==NULL){
printf("Not Changed");
}
else{
printf("%d" , *p);
return 0;
}

